.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 1039 AM PDT Sun Oct 11 2026

Hazardous conditions persist over the coastal waters due to fresh
breezes to gale force winds and rough seas. Strongest winds will
be over the outer waters north of Pigeon Point. The strong winds
and long period southerly swell will result in a confused sea
state into the beginning of next week.

&&

.BEACHES...
Issued at 1042 AM PDT Sun Oct 11 2026

Buoy reports this morning still indicated some solid swell
entering the coastal waters. As such, still seeing an energetic
the surf zone. Give the observed height and period isolated
breaking waves 18-20 ft are possible at favored break points. Long
period southerly swell will persist through the weekend, bringing
an increased risk of sneaker waves and strong rip currents. The
large tidal swings will also result in coastal erosion as water
and waves are brought farther up the beach than normal, especially
during high tide. Remain off jetties, piers, rocks, and other
waterside infrastructure as waves can sweep across the shoreline
without warning, pulling people into the sea. Remain out of the
water to avoid hazardous surf and strong rip currents and never
turn your back on the ocean!

